<%- include('partials/head', { title: 'Evensplit — split expenses, settle in fewer payments' }) %>
<%- include('partials/nav', { active: '', group: null }) %>

<main class="wrap narrow">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Split the bill. <span class="gradient-text">Settle it in fewer payments.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Add who paid for what, split it evenly or not, and Evensplit works out the shortest
      set of payments that clears everybody. Amounts are whole cents, so three people
      splitting €100 owe €33.34, €33.33 and €33.33 — never €33.33 three times with a cent
      quietly missing.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="<%= demoSlug ? '/g/' + demoSlug : '/demo' %>">Open the demo group →</a>
      <a class="btn" href="#new">Start your own</a>
    </div>
    <div class="chips">
      <span class="chip">Integer cents</span>
      <span class="chip">Uneven splits</span>
      <span class="chip">Fewest transfers</span>
      <span class="chip">No signup</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="new">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>New group</h2>
      <form method="post" action="/groups">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="name">What is it for?</label>
          <input type="text" id="name" name="name" placeholder="Lisbon weekend" maxlength="120" required />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="members">Who is in it?</label>
          <textarea id="members" name="members" rows="3" placeholder="Ana, Ben, Cal, Dee"></textarea>
          <p class="hint">One name per line, or separated by commas. You can add more later.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="field" style="max-width: 170px;">
          <label for="currency">Currency</label>
          <select id="currency" name="currency">
            <option>USD</option><option>EUR</option><option>GBP</option>
            <option>PHP</option><option>JPY</option><option>AUD</option><option>CAD</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Create group</button>
        <p class="hint">No signup. Anyone with the link can add expenses.</p>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="section-label">What is actually hard here</p>
    <h2>Three people split €100. Who gets the extra cent?</h2>
    <div class="split" style="margin-top: 18px;">
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-icon">¢</div>
        <h3>Money is an integer</h3>
        <p>Every amount is whole cents. €33.333… cannot be represented by anything that also adds back up to €100, so somebody has to be chosen.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-icon">=</div>
        <h3>Largest remainder</h3>
        <p>Floors first, then leftover cents by fractional part, ties by position — so the same expense splits the same way every time.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-icon">↘</div>
        <h3>Fewest transfers</h3>
        <p>Minimising payments means maximising zero-sum subsets, which is NP-hard. A bitmask DP solves it exactly for real-sized groups.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-icon">∑</div>
        <h3>No debt state machine</h3>
        <p>A settlement is just another term in the balance sum, so there is nothing to fall out of sync.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 18px;">
      <a href="https://github.com/0211IkeVenLouie/evensplit#the-hard-part">Read the full write-up →</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</main>
<footer class="site wrap"><span class="faint">Evensplit · Node, Postgres</span></footer>
</body></html>
